Corrected message:

Clear the mask paint target whenever a layer's mask is removed

Baking a layer's modifier stack removed its mask but left that mask
selected as the paint target; only the Layers panel's delete-mask
action cleared it. A later mask-targeted history snapshot then fell
back to copying the layer's colour pixels, and Undo could write them
over the restored mask.

Removing a mask now clears the mask paint target on every path (bake,
undo/redo, delete), so the delete-mask action no longer does it
separately. A mask-targeted snapshot of a layer with no mask now throws
instead of silently falling back to the colour surface, matching what
undo/redo of such an item already did.
